archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1569222Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1581307Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1685089Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1695413Z ^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1696579Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1697373Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1697771Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1698119Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1699343Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1699694Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1699902Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1700361Z    if you are ready to continue.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1700693Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1701109Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1701795Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1702325Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1702735Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1702922Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1703108Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1703446Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1703660Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1704096Z    can use Nix.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1704239Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1704350Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1704542Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1704845Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1705361Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1708480Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1708646Z I will:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1708966Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1709291Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1709938Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1710392Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1710799Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1711087Z  - install Nix in /nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1711355Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1711774Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1712166Z    /root
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1723797Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1724618Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1735133Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1735992Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1736822Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1737635Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1738232Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1756707Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1757245Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1768560Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1769401Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1769836Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1770103Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1770385Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1770685Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1770870Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1771353Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1771648Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1771777Z If you would like to
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1772106Z see the output, try like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1772385Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1772604Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1773092Z   $ sh ./install-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1773251Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1773261Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1773490Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1781570Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:38:14.1782041Z been installed on this system.
